@ShadowDragon
Thank you for stepping into the breach until I could fix it.  Much appreciated.
@slimmmeiske2
link now works.

@ShadowDragon
You are a star for finding these.  Those roof tiles are a nightmare to get right, so complex.
In answer to your question, the tiles are all B-E but sometimes the passability needs to change for particular tiles depending on where/how they are being used.  Then I have to block them with regions.  Clearly that particular configuration needed more adjustment.

@ShadowDragon
Argh!!! When I deployed the new version I forgot to reset the Options menu to make the quest tracker OFF instead of ON.  I hate it being on by default, big mistake on the part of VS, in my opinion.
Off I go to do another upload.

@woootbm
Not too harsh at all.  Thanks for taking the time to play this.  I agree with your point about starting combat being a bit basic atm.  Two reasons: first I am undecided how much to assume the player has found in the way of items, gear and experience; second I tend to wait on a lot of balancing until I've seen how the skills play out across the party over time.  Something that looks good at the beginning can be eclipsed later on - you know the score yourself.
I'm glad you enjoyed the story telling.  I may be a bit iffy on balancing, but I do think my writing is good.

@Sword_of_Dusk
I'm glad to hear that the town bug is sorted.  You can't get into the Abandoned Fort, it's not included in the demo.  Now I just need to work out why the regions blocking your access didn't keep you from trying to go there.
@TRIDIUM
None of the heads are RTP.  They are not, it is true, as well proportioned as Wayward Martian, but their sprites are a lot taller even than these, so it is easier for the head to look better.  btw, I forgot to mention in reply to your suggestion that I fix the splash screen, as you could see that it is a placeholder I'm not sure that it's 'fixable' until the screen is finalised.  And the other thing - I thoroughly dislike busts for dialogue because if you have a cut scene where things are happening, and people are moving about, then the busts cover that up.  I suppose it makes less difference if it's just static talking, but even then, a lot of details on the maps are covered up.  Personal preferences here for both of us.
